ring two concepts. Premise and Designing Principle: The premise is your story summarized in one sentence. In each article of the series, there will be this part where I will create a lore for an imaginary project.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/174760bac8f322ade432e12d97823e0e","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-01-26T20:23:02.561Z"},{"id":"VQk7hQNi3","title":"The Structure and Mysteries of the Story - How to Apply Storytelling to Your Project, Part 3","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/the-structure-and-mysteries-of-the-story-how-to-apply-storytelling-to-your-project-part-3","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-structure-and-mysteries-of-the-story---how-to-apply-storytelling-to-your-project-part-3-vqk7hqni3","summary":"The Structure and Mysteries of the Story - How to Apply Storytelling to Your Project, Part 3 Jan 26, 2023\u00b7 8 min read. In this article, we will have a look at the different types of structures that a story can be built with. Before this, I will introduce you to the base that all stories share.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5fabc71c5ddf9359e9befd7b82dea8b4","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-01-26T20:22:53.925Z"},{"id":"JvDBtmSzH","title":"The Theme, Values, and Moral Debate of Your Story- How to Apply Storytelling to Your Project, Part 2","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/the-theme-values-and-moral-debate-of-your-story-how-to-apply-storytelling-to-your-project-part-2","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-theme-values-and-moral-debate-of-your-story--how-to-apply-storytelling-to-your-project-part-2-jvdbtmszh","summary":"The Theme, Values, and Moral Debate of Your Story- How to Apply Storytelling to Your Project, Part 2 Jan 26, 2023\u00b7 8 min read. In the previous article Premise and Designing Principle, we learned how to create a premise, what a design principle is, and how to use a designing principle.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/0c7a349d2af58dc9c838e7fe9afec45e","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-01-26T20:22:44.598Z"},{"id":"enyPtcV05","title":"Why do protocols burn tokens?","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/why-do-protocols-burn-tokens","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-do-protocols-burn-tokens--enyptcv05","summary":"Nenad Novakovi\u0107: People have devoted their lives to amassing decentralized assets in the hopes that they\u2019ll one day become immensely wealthy when their tokens soar in value. The explanation of this practice, known as buyback & burn, relates to a simple piece of economic theory: supply and demand.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3f4cc070ba41a62a4a44b868a5c06496","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-12-28T20:27:47.040Z"},{"id":"T6sJ0snW-","title":"What is Polygon?","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/what-is-polygon","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-polygon--t6sj0snw","summary":"Polygon is a \u2018layer-2\u2019 network that helps scale the Ethereum blockchain. It sits atop Ethereum but processes transactions faster and cheaper, then feeds back transaction information to Ethereum. Polygon has since advanced to become a suite of scaling solutions, plus an independent network capable of standing on its own two feet.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/976cf7c0f6f88a991609a7800c791b4a","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-12-28T20:23:02.513Z"},{"id":"xnO1rSmvq","title":"How Polkadot Works","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/how-polkadot-works","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-polkadot-works-xno1rsmvq","summary":"Polkadot, launched in 2020, is the twelfth largest cryptocurrency with a market capitalization of $7.6 billion. At its peak in November 2021, DOT commanded a market cap of $53.21 billion. The network comprises lots of different blockchains \u2013 not just one, like Ethereum.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/041a3152d1daa1659f9361bab643906c","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-12-28T20:22:55.344Z"},{"id":"QNbMQsrZL","title":"What is Aptos?","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/what-is-aptos","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-aptos--qnbmqsrzl","summary":"Meta, formerly known as Facebook, almost got into the blockchain game in 2019. After Mark Zuckerberg abandoned the project, its developers repurposed what was left and created their own blockchain: Aptos. This article explains what it is, how it works, and why a lot of people are concerned about the way it is structured.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/0a6e8ad0821f24db40a881c9444c6489","num_upvotes":12,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2022-12-28T20:22:46.393Z"},{"id":"_wqaX4Fsz","title":"What is the Ethereum merge?","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/what-is-the-ethereum-merge","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-the-ethereum-merge---wqax4fsz","summary":"In September 2022, Ethereum transitioned from a proof of-work chain to a proof-of-stake chain. The Merge laid the groundwork for fixing the problems that slow down the beleaguered blockchain, while instantly making it 99% more energy efficient. PoW chains take the computationally intensive part of mining out of the equation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3676117f00431aa3c0e399fb727420b9","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-12-28T20:22:38.369Z"},{"id":"nZF5Qq8rY","title":"Render Network\u2019s Distributed GPU Compute to Power Metaverse","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/render-networks-distributed-gpu-compute-to-power-metaverse","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/render-network-s-distributed-gpu-compute-to-power-metaverse-nzf5qq8ry","summary":"Render Network is a decentralized network that connects those needing computer processing power with those willing to rent out unused compute capacity. Those who offer use of their device\u2019s unused graphics processing unit (GPU) are rewarded with render tokens (RNDR) The distributed network was founded in 2016 by Jules Urbach.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e0263c3a7d8b5215ad4d88d43bfc1bb8","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-12-28T20:07:22.837Z"},{"id":"g1UND9H6B","title":"ZK Proofs and Their Implications for Privacy in Crypto","url":"https://web3.hashnode.com/zk-proofs-and-their-implications-for-privacy-in-crypto","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/zk-proofs-and-their-implications-for-privacy-in-crypto-g1und9h6b","summary":"The origins of ZK proofs date back to a research paper published in 1985. For years the research failed to capture anyone\u2019s imagination as it simply hadn\u2019t found anything in the way of a practical use case. The lack of software tooling, fast hardware and alternative options prevented ZK proof from going mainstream.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/0145cd5190da79c4ff0344086657c633","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-12-28T20:02:56.837Z"}],"similar_handles":["hashnode","elmah","onmsft","ossphs","devdojo"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","hamelhusain","xai","hwchase17","sama"],"similar":[{"id":"hashnode","handle":"hashnode","name":"Hashnode","is_squad":false,"x":-6.3711,"y":4.754,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":621,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/4a287b2e7cb5499bae863f8e7137cdb4","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":6.570445,"median_upvotes":3.0,"author_present_share":0.384863,"hype_score":0.021739,"avg_read_time":5.76252,"tag_diversity":0.450886},"top_tags_preview":[["general-programming",111],["react",79],["tech-news",60]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.2059,6.0294],"cadence_depth":[9.2647,-0.2941],"hype_va